{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Dana, I checked your laptop (BL-LT-0101). The C: drive is not low: it has about 310 GB free out of 512 GB (about 60%), and the system reports no disk warnings. So the low-space message may be for a different drive, a removable or external drive, or an old notification. Could you send me the exact text of the warning and the drive letter it names, and tell me whether you still see it after a restart? If you'd like to free up space yourself in the meantime, you can empty the Recycle Bin and Downloads folder, then run Disk Cleanup from the Start menu. Once I have the details, I can take the next step.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user (user_id 1, CEO, VIP, active, usual hours 08:00-18:00 ET) and check_device_status on BL-LT-0101 (Windows 11 Pro, online, last check-in 2026-10-11 03:04 UTC). Disk: 512 GB total, 310 GB free, 60.5% free, no warnings. This does not match KB-017's trigger (under 10% free), so no cleanup was started. The warning may refer to a different volume or be stale. Asked user for the exact warning text and drive letter. Remote cleanup is not available through my tools. Next step if the warning is confirmed on a volume that is actually low: run KB-017 steps with the user and re-check. Escalate if free space on the affected volume stays under 10% after cleanup.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-017"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
